{"message":"Harden auth, fix XSS in Studio, add rate limiting, and unify embedded/HTTP core logic\n\nSecurity fixes: hash session tokens at rest with constant-time lookup, rate-limit auth endpoints, close email-enumeration timing gap in password recovery, escape all Studio-rendered row/user values (stored XSS), gate Studio behind an optional token, validate WebSocket subscribe against canAccess, stop leaking internal hook exceptions to clients, add STARTTLS/response-code checking to the built-in SMTP client.\n\nCorrectness fixes: serialize table create/alter-column per table name to close a race on concurrent first-inserts, reject ambiguous array bodies on PUT/PATCH, validate select/order against actual row columns, cap unfiltered row fetches at 50k to bound memory, add graceful SIGINT/SIGTERM shutdown.\n\nArchitecture: refactored db.ts/auth.ts/rest.ts to take an explicit libSQL Client instead of closing over a module singleton, then rewrote embedded.ts to call the exact same handleAuth/handleRest logic in-process instead of duplicating ~90 lines of CRUD/auth/filter code -- fixes were previously at risk of applying to only one of the two code paths.\n\nVerified via the real e2e suite (70/70), a new embedded-mode smoke check (11/11), and live curl/browser witnesses of rate limiting, the Studio auth gate, and the XSS fix."}
